# An application Kconfig becomes the Kconfig ROOT, so it has to source
# Kconfig.zephyr itself - and that source line must come LAST, after the
# options below, or they are not visible to a -DCONFIG_... on the command
# line.

menu "Portenta Machine Control Explorer"

config PMC_OPEN_PA1_ANALOG_SWITCH
	bool "Open the PA1 analog switch, freeing AI2 from the RMII clock"
	default y
	help
	  AI2 and the Ethernet RMII 50 MHz reference clock share the PA1/PA1_C
	  pad pair on the STM32H747, joined by a single SYSCFG analog switch.
	  Opening it separates them, which is what AI2 needs in order to read
	  anything meaningful rather than a 50 MHz clock.

	  Set this to n to leave that switch CLOSED. The only reason to do so
	  is to test whether the Ethernet MAC needs it closed to receive its
	  reference clock - with it closed, AI2 is measuring the clock and its
	  readings are meaningless. PC2 and PC3 are unaffected either way, so
	  AI0 and AI1 keep working regardless.

	  This is a genuine either/or if it turns out the clock arrives on the
	  PA1_C ball: one pad pair cannot serve an analog input and a 50 MHz
	  clock at the same time. See docs/MEASURED.md.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
